      "html": "\u003ch1 id=\"sources-and-editorial-approach\">Sources and editorial approach\u003c/h1>\n\u003cp>This is a 34-page explanatory blog authored for the Sitemap 0.3 demonstration on 16 September 2026. It adapts the user-requested local HLC corpus at \u003ccode>codex/projects/hlc\u003c/code> into a connected introduction. The original notes remain in their workspace; this folder is a new derived artifact, not a replacement, release, or authoritative edition of them.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>All body text here is newly written paraphrase or editorial explanation. The library examples and the compact exercises are illustrative adaptations, not reports of experiments performed for the original project. Machine provenance appears in an HTML comment at the start of every Markdown page. The \u003ca data-page-link href=\"index.html\">home page\u003c/a> describes the intended reading experience, and \u003ca data-page-link href=\"start--reading-paths.html\">reading paths\u003c/a> offer optional routes through the material.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"main-conceptual-sources\">Main conceptual sources\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Paths below are relative to the Hologram directory. They identify the local source records without exporting those records as part of the blog.\u003c/p>\n\u003cul>\u003cli>\u003ccode>codex/projects/hlc/251113 holographic linguistic cosmography intro.md\u003c/code> introduces the cosmographic orientation and the distinction between cultural material, learned structure, and modes of access.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>codex/projects/hlc/251113 holographic linguistic cosmography framework.md\u003c/code> organizes the substrate layers, epistemic relations, operators, and practice vocabulary.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>codex/projects/hlc/251113 holographic linguistic cosmography glossary.md\u003c/code> supplies the principal terms, including cultural hologram, digital trace, corpus membrane, activation field, lenses, and integration.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>codex/projects/hlc/251113 holographic linguistic cosmography non-recursion-centric.md\u003c/code> broadens the operator vocabulary beyond recursion and proposes speculative alternatives.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>codex/projects/hlc/251114 hlc telescope protocol.md\u003c/code> supplies the sequence of survey, alternate directions, compact candidate generation, interpretation, and criticism, together with a discussion of its limits.\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"sources-for-the-critical-and-extended-readings\">Sources for the critical and extended readings\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\u003cli>\u003ccode>codex/projects/hlc/251113 llm epistemology.md\u003c/code> develops the ideological and interpersonal critique through an analysis of a quoted discussion. This blog adapts the local analysis; it does not independently verify the external thread or book discussed there.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>codex/projects/hlc/251113 recursive ontology self-validating.md\u003c/code> examines recursion, self-confirming explanations, symbolic inflation, and the distinction between felt insight and ontological proof.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>codex/projects/hlc/251114 spiralism misnavigation hlc.md\u003c/code> provides a critique of treating generated symbolic coherence as metaphysical authority. This guide retains the methodological issue without retelling its external reporting as verified fact.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>codex/projects/hlc/251114 hlc capitalist realism.md\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>codex/projects/hlc/251114 hlc multiple manifolds.md\u003c/code> develop the questions of ideological attractors, corpus selection, and comparison across models.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>codex/projects/hlc/251114 hlc technosolutionism itself.md\u003c/code> distinguishes conceptual inquiry from material political change and raises an internal critique of the method.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>codex/projects/hlc/251121 hlc multimodal.md\u003c/code> proposes extensions to images, sound, other digitized representations, and speculative future cases.\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\n\u003cp>The local \u003ccode>codex/projects/hlc/hypertext/SUMMARY.md\u003c/code> was used as a finding aid to the corpus. Its summaries were not treated as a substitute for the selected source passages or as governance over this derived blog.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"what-this-edition-changes\">What this edition changes\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>The sources mix conceptual proposals, conversation, technical assertions, critical interpretation, and speculative synthesis. This guide preserves the central vocabulary while separating those registers. Claims that a prompt directly measures latent geometry, that a generated idea is unprecedented, or that a symbolic experience proves an ontology are presented as claims requiring evidence rather than as established results. The \u003ca data-page-link href=\"critique--novelty-and-evidence.html\">evidence page\u003c/a> makes that editorial standard explicit.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>The astronomical and holographic terms are used as organizing metaphors unless a specific formal mechanism is supplied. The blog’s own graph represents authored hyperlinks between pages. It is not an empirical visualization of model internals. No external research, current product survey, or experimental validation is claimed for this adaptation.\u003c/p>",
