      "wordCount": 256,
      "html": "\u003ch1 id=\"three-ways-through-the-field-guide\">Three ways through the field guide\u003c/h1>\n\u003cp>A linked guide can be read as a sequence or as a set of crossings. The routes below provide a starting order without turning the folder tree into a conceptual hierarchy. The same topic can belong to more than one route: evidence is part of creativity, and politics is part of how an instrument is built.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"a-first-orientation\">A first orientation\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Start with \u003ca data-page-link href=\"start--what-is-hlc.html\">What is HLC?\u003c/a>, then move through the \u003ca data-page-link href=\"foundations--cultural-hologram.html\">cultural hologram\u003c/a>, \u003ca data-page-link href=\"foundations--digital-trace.html\">digital trace\u003c/a>, and \u003ca data-page-link href=\"foundations--latent-manifold.html\">latent manifold\u003c/a>. Finish with the \u003ca data-page-link href=\"foundations--activation-field.html\">activation field\u003c/a> to see why a generated answer depends on a particular interaction rather than simply exposing a stored world.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"a-working-session\">A working session\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Read \u003ca data-page-link href=\"practice--epistemic-posture.html\">Epistemic posture\u003c/a> and the \u003ca data-page-link href=\"practice--telescope-protocol.html\">telescope protocol\u003c/a>. Run the \u003ca data-page-link href=\"practice--exercises--attractor-survey.html\">attractor survey\u003c/a> on a small topic, then try a \u003ca data-page-link href=\"practice--exercises--boundary-search.html\">boundary search\u003c/a>. Close the session with \u003ca data-page-link href=\"practice--exercises--integration.html\">integration\u003c/a>, even if the result is a useful rejection rather than a new concept.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"a-critical-reading\">A critical reading\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Begin with \u003ca data-page-link href=\"critique--persona.html\">Persona and the feeling of an interlocutor\u003c/a>, then examine \u003ca data-page-link href=\"critique--novelty-and-evidence.html\">novelty and evidence\u003c/a>, \u003ca data-page-link href=\"critique--recursive-loops.html\">recursive loops\u003c/a>, and \u003ca data-page-link href=\"critique--ideology-and-power.html\">ideology and power\u003c/a>. The question in \u003ca data-page-link href=\"critique--technosolutionism.html\">Can a telescope become a solution?\u003c/a> brings these limits back to the purposes of the practice.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>You can also take one word as your entry point. “Attractor” connects a description of recurring output to a way of surveying assumptions. “Void” connects sparse records to the temptation to fill absence with fluent invention. “Integration” connects an exciting session to an artifact another person can examine. Follow the links that make your current question more precise, then return to \u003ca data-page-link href=\"index.html\">the home page\u003c/a> when you want another route.\u003c/p>",
